# The item 160 and 161 lines sit AFTER the lamps on purpose: a runtime older than item mode-leds
# reads only the first 16 KB of a port, and everything it understands must stay inside that.
# ---- item 160: the game's own rules, a shot that COUNTS AS one of theirs (MODE_SDK.md "Counts as") ------
# cmode_manager_get(manager, id) -> the rule's object (cmp r1,#26; push {r3,lr}: 27 rules, ids 0..26); the
# manager is `data stock_mode_manager` above. Read off this build's ELF (ea8c6d36) and emulator-proven by
# item 158's probe, which wraps the same slots: START v[8], the shot handler v[42] (this build added a slot
# at 41: Pro 1.15's is v[41]), the active query v[14], the lit-shot query v[25]; the per-player lit mask is
# the u64 at obj + 0x18 + 8 * player. Each `rule` names a rule the runtime may wrap: its id, its vtable
# pointer (checked against the object the manager returns before anything is written) and a label.
site stock_rule_get   0x000d3fa0 0xe351001a 0xe92d4008
value stock_slot_shot   42
value stock_slot_active 14
value stock_slot_lit    25
value stock_field       0x18
